// Mystery-o-matic: the arctic base murder (Jeremy's first authored case).
// Frida, Carol and Dave are stranded in an abandoned arctic military base
// during a blizzard. Dave was murdered in the command center between 4:00
// and 5:45. The murderer was alone with the victim; the body never moved;
// the murderer wasn't caught with the body.
//
// Weapon elimination (from the body):
//   poison (command center)  — ruled out: no poisoning
//   screwdriver (radio room) — ruled out: no stab wounds
//   hammer (armory)          — ruled out: no contusions
//   pistol (barracks)        — the murder weapon

theme noir
clock 4:45 minute(0.5)   // the story starts at 4:45; a minute lasts half a second

// the floor plan IS the adjacency graph: each connection declared once —
// door(to) carves both walls and names the doorway (command_center-barracks-door)
room command_center size(4 2.5 4) at(-2.2 0 -2.2) door(to barracks 1.1) door(to armory 1.1) door(to radio_room 1.1) color(purple)
room radio_room size(8.5 2.5 4) at(0.0 0 -6.6) door(to barracks 1.1) color(red)
room barracks size(4 2.5 4) at(2.2 0 -2.2) color(blue)
room armory size(4 2.5 4) at(-2.2 0 2.2) color(white)

// the weapon, where the killer found it
box footlocker size(0.8 0.5 0.5) in(barracks) at(1.4 0.25 1.2) color(#3a3f4a)
box pistol size(0.3 0.1 0.2) on(footlocker) in(barracks) color(grey)

// 4:45 — Frida: "Spotted Dave arriving while I was in the command center."
// People live at the top level and walk between rooms by name.
cylinder frida r(0.25) h(1.6) at(-3.2 0.8 -2.2) color(#c778c7)
cylinder carol r(0.25) h(1.6) at(-1.2 0.8 -2.2) color(#5b8dd9)
cylinder dave  r(0.25) h(1.6) at(-2.2 0.8 0.9) appear(4:45) color(grey)
walk dave to(command_center) over(3m)             // in through the armory door

// Frida heads for the radio room; from its center, the doorways don't
// line up — she can see nothing of what happens next.
walk frida to(command_center-radio_room-door) start(4:53) over(4m)
walk frida to(radio_room) over(2m)

// 5:15 — death was by now. Carol is alone with Dave, unobserved.
turn dave to(90 0 0) start(5:15) over(1m) ease(in)     // topple...
move dave by(0 -0.55 0) start(5:15) over(1m) ease(in)  // ...and land

// 5:45 — everyone's known position: Frida and Carol in the barracks,
// Dave's body alone in the command center.
walk frida to(radio_room-barracks-door) start(5:36) over(3m)
walk frida to(1.8 -2.2) over(4m)
walk carol to(command_center-barracks-door) start(5:39) over(3m)
walk carol to(3.8 -2.2) over(3m)

// interrogate the case — quantified answers speak wall-clock time:
? when sees(frida dave)    // her eyes are off dave across the death at 5:15
? when sees(frida carol)   // ...and off carol: the killer was unobserved
? when in(carol command_center)
? ever sees(frida dave)    // frida saw the body later: the discovery
? distance(carol pistol)

// and assert the testimony — a failing check is a compile error naming
// the violating times, so this scene PROVES its own case file:
check in(dave command_center) at(5:15)                  // the body, where it must be
check never in(frida command_center) during(5:00 5:40)  // frida gone across the murder window
check always in(carol command_center) during(4:50 5:40) // carol never left the victim
check never sees(frida dave) during(5:10 5:20)          // no one witnessed the death

// sets quantify over people ("someone", "no one") in one line:
set crew frida carol dave
check always in(crew command_center)                    // the room was never unattended
check never in(crew armory) except(dave)                // only dave ever passed the armory
